entry.summary:
This is a submission for the Hacktoberfest Weekend Challenge: Build for a Friend.
I built JobFit Local for a very specific friend: future me, the version of me opening the next job application and wondering whether a role is genuinely worth pursuing.
That person has three problems:
job descriptions are noisy and repetitive;
tailoring every application takes time;
a resume contains personal information that should not be sent to another API just to get a match score.
JobFit Local compares a resume with a job description and returns:
a semantic fit score;
skills already aligned with the role;
named skills that need honest evidence;
three practical next steps for tailoring the application.
It also explicitly warns users not to add skills they cannot defend. This is a decision aid, not a hirin…
